  "question": {
    "text": "The resistances of the platinum wire of a platinum resistance thermometer at the ice point and steam point are $8 \\Omega$ and $10 \\Omega$ respectively. After inserting in a hot bath of temperature $400^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the resistance of platinum wire is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$10 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$8 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$16 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $R_0=8 \\Omega, R_{100}=10 \\Omega$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{R}_{100}=\\mathrm{R}_0(1+\\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T})$<br />Also, $R_{400}=R_0\\left(1+\\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T}^1\\right)$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore 10=8(1+\\alpha \\times 100) \\Rightarrow 100 \\alpha=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{R}_{400}=8(1+400 \\alpha)=8(1+1)=16 \\Omega\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}